['C01','Audit timeliness','Every single audit reporting package for FY2016-FY2025 was accepted by the Federal Audit Clearinghouse after March 31 of the following year, the standard nine-month date. The delay was 12 days for FY2016, 99 days for FY2018, 64 days for FY2024 and 113 days for FY2025, and 290 days or more for FY2017 and FY2019-FY2023; the FY2021 package was accepted on 2025-01-14, about 42 months after year end.',V,'AUDIT-FY2021 ; ECFR-512','FAC acceptance dates in table 11; 2 CFR 200.512(a)(1)','The federal acceptance date can trail submission by some days. Federal COVID-19 guidance allowed extensions for fiscal years ending through June 30, 2021, so lateness against an extended date is not computed for FY2019-FY2021. The Director of Budget and Finance described the audit as performed "in a timely and collaborative manner" on 2025-07-28 (joint Finance Committee and Select Board minutes of that date, p. 3).'],
